Parkinson’s Disease (PD) is a progressive neurodegenerative disorder characterized by motor symptoms, e.g., tremor, bradykinesia, rigidity, and postural instability, alongside non-motor manifestations including cognitive decline, depression, and sleep disturbances, all severely impacting quality of life [1]. Affecting over 10 million people worldwide, with nearly one million cases in the United States alone, PD poses a ma
